# 5. Service + repository save (and entity setters that mutate on assignment)

`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner` — `src/main/java/.../service/ClinicServiceImpl.java:232-237`:

```java
    @Override
    @Transactional
    public void saveOwner(Owner owner) throws DataAccessException {
        ownerRepository.save(owner);
    }
```

`@Transactional` (Spring's `org.springframework.transaction.annotation.Transactional`) — read-write. `findAllOwners` (called earlier by the controller) is `@Transactional(readOnly = true)` (`:126-129`).

Repository: `OwnerRepository.save` interface — `src/main/java/.../repository/OwnerRepository.java:66`. Active implementation is Spring Data's auto-generated proxy for `SpringDataOwnerRepository` (`repository/springdatajpa/SpringDataOwnerRepository.java:36-37`, `@Profile("spring-data-jpa")`); it declares no custom `save` (inherited/generated). No cache annotations, no explicit event publication.

Entity save target — `Owner` (`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`). Note two setters normalize/mutate values whenever assigned (these run during MapStruct mapping / assignment, not as JPA callbacks):
- `setEmail` (`:163-165`): lower-cases via `toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT)`.
- `setRegistrationDate` (`:180-182`): defaults `null`→`LocalDate.now()`, then `BusinessDay.adjust(...)` rolls forward off weekends/holidays (`model/BusinessDay.java:41-46`; holiday set `:28-31`).

Persistent constraints on the entity (checked by Hibernate/BeanValidation at persist): `Owner.address @NotEmpty` (`:44-46`), `Owner.city @NotEmpty` (`:54-56`), `Owner.telephone @NotEmpty @Pattern(regexp="^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$")` (`:58-61`); inherited `Person.firstName @NotEmpty` and `Person.lastName @NotEmpty` (`model/Person.java:31-37`). Id generation: `BaseEntity` `@Id @GeneratedValue(strategy = IDENTITY)` (`model/BaseEntity.java:33-35`). Many enrichment fields (`memberId`, `namesakeCount`, `bulkSignupWarning`, `capacityWarning`, `householdSize`, `possibleDuplicateOf`, `membershipLevel`, `title`, `addressLine1/2`) are `@Transient` (not persisted; `Owner.java:38-97`). `Owner.pets` is `@OneToMany(cascade = ALL, mappedBy="owner", fetch=EAGER)` (`:99-100`).

No `@PrePersist`/`@PostPersist`/`@PreUpdate`/entity listeners exist on `Owner` or any entity.

