# 6b. Exception handling advice that applies to this endpoint

`RejectedRequestAdvice` — `src/main/java/.../rest/advice/RejectedRequestAdvice.java:37-68`: `@RestControllerAdvice @Order(HIGHEST_PRECEDENCE)`; `@ExceptionHandler(RejectedRequestException.class)` renders the business-rule rejections (429/409 from the controller guards) as RFC-7807 problem+json, preserving the status. Also defines the `RejectedRequestException(status, detail)` class.

`ExceptionControllerAdvice` — `src/main/java/.../rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java:48-184`: `@ControllerAdvice` with:
- `@ExceptionHandler(MethodArgumentNotValidException.class)` (`:149-182`) → 400, builds `schemaValidationErrors` and an `errors` list from field errors (this is what fires when the `OwnerFieldsDto` Bean Validation fails).
- `@ExceptionHandler(IllegalArgumentException.class)` (`:134-140`) → 400 (this catches the mapper/validator throws: telephone, postcode, registration date, disposable email, blank address).
- `@ExceptionHandler(DataIntegrityViolationException.class)` (`:112-123`) → 404.
- `@ExceptionHandler(AccessDeniedException.class)` (`:83-86`) → re-thrown so Spring Security handles 403.
- `@ExceptionHandler(Exception.class)` (`:95-102`) → 500.

