# Aspects / filters / interceptors

`CallMonitoringAspect` — `src/main/java/.../util/CallMonitoringAspect.java:37-95`: `@Aspect`, `@Around("within(@org.springframework.stereotype.Repository *)")` times and counts calls. Per its own class Javadoc, Spring-Data-JPA repository proxies are not annotated `@Repository`, so under the active `spring-data-jpa` profile it does not advise the owner save path. No servlet `Filter`, `OncePerRequestFilter`, or `HandlerInterceptor` classes exist in the project (only Spring Security's default chain enforces the `@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")` on the controller methods).
